ans  have been joking about  since the first film was released in  1977  and was most notably marked in a star  wars parody episode of family guy blue  harvest  so anyway i says forget the dental plan  forget sick leave  i just want a railing you know one  railing right here  another hilarious moment of  self-deprecation in the mandalorian  happens during the cold open of chapter  8 which shows two stormtroopers missing  repeatedly  while firing at a piece of scrap within  close range the scenes playing on the  age-old trope of the notoriously bad  blaster  aim for a guy who never shows his face  din jaron is a huge chick magnet younger  viewers may not notice  but mature audiences will pick up on the  fact that excluding cara dune  the few non-mandalorian females he's  crossed paths with have either been  instantly attracted to him or had some  sort of romantic history with him  in chapter 4 the sanctuary din cross has  passed with a young widow named omara  who seems to want the warrior to settle  down with her bad boy mando also seems  to have broken the heart of xi'an  a knife throwing twilight he works with  in chapter 6 the prisoner  she threatens to use her blades against  him for whatever shenanigans he pulled  on her in the past  adults will likely appreciate the sheer  irony of seeing comedian bill burr cast  in a star wars related role  longtime fans of his podcasts know that  the snarky bostonian has long riffed on  the franchise as he never forged a  personal connection with the original  trilogy  when it was released in his youth burst  stirred up controversy within the star  wars fandom for remarks he made in 2015  declaring that when he did finally watch  the original trilogy in his mid-20s  he wasn't impressed i read a quote that  you had this is a while back i think he  called star wars a cheesy self-help book  put in outer space with much outer space  yeah to be fair bill makes fun of  everyone and everything equally  even his beloved sports team 