re  grogu came from  if he's not a clone as has been implied  in the show thus far then he was  spontaneously created like anakin  skywalker  or he was made the old-fashioned way so  far the only other creatures encountered  like grogu and star wars have been yoda  and yaddle could grogu's existence  explain the latter's sudden  disappearance from the jedi height  council that all remains fan theory for  now  but regardless of who sired the being  formerly known as baby yoda the twisted  adult mind can't help but wonder how  such creatures would accomplish  procreation  awkward it would be yes a pleasant image  it is not  unless you know some kids with very  strange and mature tastes they likely  missed a quick mandalorian reference to  the classic comedy office space  the film parodies all the negative  aspects of toiling away at the dreaded  9-5  cube farm from horrible bosses and  wasting away in traffic  anyone who has ever worked a less than  desirable job can relate to this movie  office space  also makes fun of unnecessary corporate  bureaucracy and paperwork  symbolized by the dreaded tps reports  and the film it's just we're putting new  cover sheets on all the tps reports  before they go out now so if you could  go ahead and  try to remember to do that from now on  that'd be great these reports  seem to have made their way into the  star wars universe because mayfeld  mentions them in chapter 15 the believer  it's such a quick line and easy to miss  come on let's go fill out those tps  reports so we can go recharge the power  coil and you thought the empire was evil  before  chapter 15 is loaded with quentin  tarantino references  mayfeld and mando find themselves in a  dangerous situation  while posing as empire personnel when  officer valen hest insists they join him  for a drink  they risk exposing themselves while  swapping small talk but they can't break  rank by refusing hesse's offer  so they agree the suspenseful scene is  reminiscent of the hair-raisingly  intense bar scene in inglorious bastards  both feature characters infiltrating  enemy cultures while attempting to blend  in as natives  and both situations soon explode into a  violent catastrophe  mando and mayfeld frolic at the empire  bar might also remind an adult viewer of  a scene from django unchained  when dr schultz gives calvin candy a  bullet rather than a requested handshake  just like schultz mayfeld is so overcome  with loathing he can't help but pull the  trigger  and thus puts his companion in grave  danger also like candy hess  has a thick southern accent and a  sinister yet lackadaisical demeanor  a towering villain requires an actor of  serious skill luckily the mandalorians  violin hess is played by a highly  accomplished actor  adults will likely recognize richard  brake brakes succeeds in making his  character absolutely hateful but then as  grown-ups know he has a lot of  experience in that department  break started his acting career in 1993  with a small part as a reporter in a  british comedy drama tv series  jeeves and worcester since then break  has performed in dozens of projects and  at least 30 films spanning all genres  one of his more memorable roles to date  has also been one of his most brief  he was cast as a night king in the  fourth and fifth seasons  of game of thrones check out one of our  newest videos right here plus even more  looper videos about your favorite shows  are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]  you

